<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vasily of Kostroma</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1241">1241</a>–<a href="/years/1276">1276</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vasily of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kostroma">Kostroma</a> was the youngest son of Grand Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaroslav-ii-of-vladimir">Yaroslav II of Vladimir</a> and the first prince of Kostroma, which he received as his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanage</a> after his father's death in 1246. He fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuanians">Lithuanians</a> and the Novgorodians, and in 1272 became grand prince of Vladimir with the approval of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a>, ruling from Kostroma rather than Vladimir. He also held Novgorod, and died in 1276.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vasily-of-kostroma.jpg" alt="Vasily of Kostroma" width="320" height="419" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vasily_Yaroslavich_of_Kostroma_-_fragment_from_%22Our_Lady_Feodorovskaya_in_Miracles%22.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
